    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">hanging sleeve</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">Long loose sleeves with a slit through which the arm can emerge. Also, long false decorative sleeves attached to the back of the armhole. Worn by men, women, or children especially from the 15th through the 18th century.</dcterms:description>
  </rdf:Description>
